# exp37_s2_both LoRA dropout comparison

Single inference seed (42), 20,000 paired test samples, ten-map equal-weight macro. Differences are descriptive; no statistical significance claim.

- Baseline (dropout on): `/data/home/jiahao/UniLIP_outputs/outputs_eval/benchmark_v2/exp37_s2_both/checkpoint-6000/test/seed_42/infer_bs8/discrete`
- Candidate (dropout off): `/data/home/jiahao/UniLIP_outputs/outputs_eval/benchmark_v2/exp37_s2_both/checkpoint-6000/test/seed_42/infer_bs8/lora_dropout_off/discrete`
- Checkpoint: `outputs/csgo_1b/exp37_s2_both/checkpoint-6000/model.safetensors`; LoRA dropout modules: 438

`Δ = off − on`. Higher is better for PSNR, SSIM, Boundary_F1, CLIP; lower is better for LPIPS, Pixel_MAE_255, FID.

